## A long name pinned to the loopback address, not -sname. The node is only
## reachable there anyway, and naming it 127.0.0.1 is what lets observer on a
## laptop connect straight through an SSH tunnel with no hostname to resolve.
-name freewhen@127.0.0.1
-setcookie freewhen_local

## Distribution exists so that an operator can attach a remote_console on the
## machine, and so that observer can be pointed at it over an SSH tunnel.
## Bound to loopback the cookie above is not a secret, and epmd is not
## reachable from the network. The port is pinned because a tunnel cannot
## forward a port chosen at random.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 9100
-kernel inet_dist_listen_max 9100

## Rooms are RAM-only and short-lived; a crash dump would be the one artifact
## that outlives them. Zero retention means zero crash dumps.
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP /dev/null
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS 0

+K true
+A 8
## Bound the atom table: room hashes and aliases must never become atoms.
+t 1048576
